title: Ade almost paid a scholarship scammer
caption: Ade almost paid $300 to "secure" a scholarship 😬 Real scholarships NEVER ask you to pay to win them. Share this with a friend who's applying 🙏 #scholarship #scamalert #studyabroad #storytime
hook: DON'T PAY FOR A "SCHOLARSHIP"! | ADE & QUDDUS
cta: STAY SAFE | 2705 Only apply on official websites | 1f6a8 Never pay to "secure" a scholarship
ctasay: Comment SAFE if you've seen a scam like this, and share this with a friend who's applying.
bye: Follow so nobody scams you again!
cast: ade

== street | NIGHT · CITY STREET | busy African city street at night with colorful shop lights and wet road | walkin
ade (cheer): Quddus! I won a scholarship to Canada! Full funding, flight, everything!
quddus (wave): Congratulations, Ade! Which university?
ade (shrug): They didn't say yet. But the agent said I just need to pay three hundred dollars to secure my slot.
quddus (shock): Ade. Put the phone down. Slowly.
ade (worried): Why? He sounded very nice. He even used five emojis.

== living | ADE'S LIVING ROOM | cozy African living room with a sofa, plants and evening light through the window | sofa
quddus (talk): Listen. Real scholarships never ask you to pay money to win them or to secure a slot.
> 1f6a8 | SCAM RED FLAGS | 1f4b8 Pay a fee to secure your scholarship | 23f0 You won something you never applied for | 1f4f1 Only talks on WhatsApp, no official email
ade (think): But how do I know which ones are real?
quddus (point): Check the official website. A real university or government scholarship has its own page, and you apply there, not through a random agent.
> 2705 | HOW TO CHECK | 1f310 Find it on the official website | 1f4e9 Official email domain, not Gmail | 1f50e Search the name plus the word scam
ade (facepalm): So the scholarship that found me on WhatsApp at midnight was not real.
quddus (thumbs): Exactly. Opportunities don't chase you in your DMs. You apply for them.
ade (worried): Okay. I'm blocking him. Then I'm reporting him.
quddus (talk): Good. And next time, send me the link before you send anyone money.
ade (cheer): Deal! My three hundred dollars says thank you.
